TITLE:
Aegir Deep Sea Expedition — Interview Transcript #03

SOURCE:
AEDSE-ER / Deep Sea Observation Division

STATUS:
ROUTINE | CLASSIFICATION: MUNDANE

LOCATION:
Aegir Deep Sea Research Vessel "Nereid"

DEPTH:
11,030m below sea level

DATE:
████████████


============================================================

INTERVIEW RECORD

INTERVIEWER:
Research Officer █████

SUBJECT:
Expedition Lead █████
Aegir Deep Sea Expedition Team

============================================================


[BEGIN TRANSCRIPT]


INTERVIEWER:

The final report states that the expedition reached a depth
of 11,030 meters.

Can you confirm this figure?


SUBJECT:

Confirmed.

The descent lasted seventeen hours.

At that depth, the pressure outside the vessel was beyond
anything most surface engineers would consider survivable.

But the hull remained stable.


INTERVIEWER:

The report mentions that 2,847 specimens were collected.

What was the purpose of collecting such a large number?


SUBJECT:

At first, classification.

That was the official answer.

We wanted to understand what survived down there.

The organisms.

The minerals.

The changes caused by the environment.


INTERVIEWER:

And unofficially?


SUBJECT:

...

Understanding whether they were surviving.

Or waiting.


INTERVIEWER:

Waiting?


SUBJECT:

The deep sea is not empty.

People on the surface imagine darkness as absence.

They are wrong.

Darkness is simply a place where something else has adapted.


INTERVIEWER:

The report also mentions three anomalies detected during
the expedition.

Could you elaborate?


SUBJECT:

No.


INTERVIEWER:

The data is classified only as "UNDER REVIEW".

There is no security restriction.


SUBJECT:

There should be.


INTERVIEWER:

Why?


SUBJECT:

Because the first anomaly was a signal.

The second was a structure.

The third...


[RECORD INTERRUPTION]


INTERVIEWER:

The third anomaly?


SUBJECT:

We received a response.


INTERVIEWER:

From what?


SUBJECT:

...


SUBJECT:

That is the wrong question.


INTERVIEWER:

What is the correct question?


SUBJECT:

Ocean is roaring.


============================================================

[END TRANSCRIPT]


